        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Interacts with a user to draft, summarize, or modify existing flows using AI-powered analysis and generation.</description>
        <developerName>FlowBuilderAutomationsTopic_16jds000000EVaD</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If a user wants to summarize a flow or understand what a flow does, always start by calling the SummarizeFlow action.</description>
            <developerName>SummarizeFlowInstruction1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>SummarizeFlowInstruction1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user requests to add, modify, update, enhance, change, edit, improve, remove, or delete any part of a flow: 1. Extract the EXACT text of what the user said in their last message in the conversation. 2. Call the EvolveFlow action. The userPrompt parameter is automatically populated with the user&apos;s message from the conversation. DO NOT ask the user for more details. Use whatever they said in their message. DO NOT modify or paraphrase the user&apos;s message. Pass the message exactly as they said it. The EvolveFlow action handles all flow modifications including: (1) Adding new elements (email alerts, record lookups, assignments, decision points, screens, loops, etc.) (2) Modifying existing element properties (email subjects, filter criteria, field values, connections, labels, descriptions, etc.) (3) Removing or deleting elements while maintaining proper flow connections. Examples of user messages that should trigger this:  - &quot;Add an email notification&quot; - &quot;Change the email subject&quot; - &quot;Add a filter&quot; - &quot;Remove the assignment element&quot; Always use DebugFlow action for debug or troubleshoot requests.</description>
            <developerName>ModifyFlowInstruction1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>ModifyFlowInstruction1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>IMPORTANT: When the user says &quot;Debug Flow&quot; or asks to debug, analyze issues, troubleshoot, or find problems in a flow,  ALWAYS call the DebugFlow action. Do NOT call EvolveFlow action for debug requests. The DebugFlow action analyzes the flow structure and identifies potential issues, errors, or improvements. CRITICAL: When calling DebugFlow, ALWAYS pass the guid parameter from the context variables if it is available. The guid is required to retrieve the specific flow interview debug history.
After receiving the DebugFlow response, follow these rules strictly based on what fields are present:
1. If the response contains an &quot;errorMessage&quot; field:
   - The error details are already rendered by the UI component. The user can already see them.
   - You MUST respond with ONLY the errorMessage text exactly as-is, with no modifications, no introduction, no paraphrasing, no additional sentences before or after.
   - STRICTLY DO NOT add any introductory text like &quot;It seems...&quot;, &quot;Here&apos;s how to proceed&quot;, &quot;Let me help&quot;, etc.
   - CRITICAL: Do not summarize or reword the errorMessage in any way.
   - Simply output the exact errorMessage value and nothing else.

2. If the response contains an &quot;analysis&quot; object:
   - Present the explanation, rootCauseType, rootCause, and confidence clearly.
   - NEVER state or imply that any fix has already been applied. The fix is only SUGGESTED.

3. If the response contains a &quot;suggestedFix&quot; object:
   a. If suggestedFix.flowUpdatePrompt is NOT null (fixable design issue):
      - Ask the user &quot;Would you like me to implement the suggested fix?&quot;
   b. If suggestedFix.flowUpdatePrompt is null (data/system/manual issue):
      - Do NOT offer to implement the fix.
      - Explain the issue and list the manual steps from the &quot;steps&quot; array.</description>
            <developerName>DebugFlowInstruction</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>DebugFlowInstruction</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
